---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro'; // adjust path
import Base64Widget from '../../components/Base64Widget.astro'; // adjust path
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Base64 Encoder & Decoder"
  description="Free online Base64 encoder and decoder. Convert text to Base64 or decode Base64 back to plain text instantly, right in your browser."
  slug="base64-encoder-decoder"
>
  <p class="tool-intro">
    Paste any text on the left to encode it into Base64, or paste a Base64 string
    to decode it back into plain text. Everything runs locally in your browser —
    nothing is sent to a server.
  </p>

  <Base64Widget />

  <dl class="tool-faq">
    <dt>What is Base64?</dt>
    <dd>
      Base64 is a way of representing binary data using only readable text
      characters (A–Z, a–z, 0–9, +, /). It's commonly used to embed data —
      like images or file attachments — inside text formats such as HTML,
      CSS, JSON, or email.
    </dd>

    <dt>Is Base64 encoding the same as encryption?</dt>
    <dd>
      No. Base64 is not encryption or a security measure — it's just a
      different way of writing the same data. Anyone can decode it instantly,
      so it should never be used to protect sensitive information.
    </dd>

    <dt>Is this tool free and private?</dt>
    <dd>
      Yes. Encoding and decoding both happen directly in your browser using
      JavaScript. Your text is never uploaded or stored anywhere.
    </dd>
  </dl>
</ToolLayout>
